WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.025
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:08.619
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.919 --> 00:00:15.367
Unit twenty-four: Debating Global Issues. Today you will organise arguments with linking words.

4
00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.447
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.586
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.242
Debate.

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.225
Debate means a formal discussion with two sides.

8
00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:31.269
We had a debate about school uniforms.

9
00:00:31.883 --> 00:00:34.176
Your turn. Say: Debate.

10
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:37.814
Debate.

11
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.365
Motion.

12
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.872
Motion means the topic of a formal debate.

13
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:45.587
The motion is 'Homework should be banned'.

14
00:00:46.183 --> 00:00:48.406
Your turn. Say: Motion.

15
00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:52.059
Motion.

16
00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:53.702
Argument.

17
00:00:54.717 --> 00:00:57.320
Argument means a reason that supports a point.

18
00:00:57.917 --> 00:00:59.533
Give one strong argument.

19
00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:02.351
Your turn. Say: Argument.

20
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.155
Argument.

21
00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:07.767
Rebuttal.

22
00:01:08.783 --> 00:01:12.014
Rebuttal means an answer that shows the other side is wrong.

23
00:01:12.617 --> 00:01:14.175
Her rebuttal won the debate.

24
00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:17.598
Your turn. Say: Rebuttal.

25
00:01:20.433 --> 00:01:21.318
Rebuttal.

26
00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:23.096
Evidence.

27
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.605
Evidence means facts that support an argument.

28
00:01:27.217 --> 00:01:29.193
Use evidence, not feelings.

29
00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:31.983
Your turn. Say: Evidence.

30
00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:35.846
Evidence.

31
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:37.573
Persuasive.

32
00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:41.291
Persuasive means able to make people agree.

33
00:01:41.883 --> 00:01:43.906
His speech was very persuasive.

34
00:01:44.517 --> 00:01:47.285
Your turn. Say: Persuasive.

35
00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.285
Persuasive.

36
00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.005
Audience.

37
00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:56.132
Audience means the people who listen.

38
00:01:56.717 --> 00:01:58.589
Look at the audience when you speak.

39
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:01.917
Your turn. Say: Audience.

40
00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:05.745
Audience.

41
00:02:06.483 --> 00:02:07.461
Respect.

42
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:11.309
Respect means treating others' views as important.

43
00:02:11.917 --> 00:02:13.696
Always debate with respect.

44
00:02:14.283 --> 00:02:16.611
Your turn. Say: Respect.

45
00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:20.433
Respect.

46
00:02:21.233 --> 00:02:25.314
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:29.998
Visal, the motion is 'Plastic bags should be banned'. Start.

48
00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:37.068
Firstly, plastic harms sea animals. Moreover, it takes hundreds of years to break down.

49
00:02:38.183 --> 00:02:39.684
What about the other side?

50
00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:45.209
On the other hand, some people say paper bags cost more.

51
00:02:46.317 --> 00:02:47.434
Your rebuttal?

52
00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:54.082
However, reusable bags are cheap. In conclusion, the ban is a good idea.

53
00:02:55.233 --> 00:02:56.525
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:57.383 --> 00:03:00.683
Grammar focus: Linking words for arguments.

55
00:03:00.983 --> 00:03:02.240
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:07.286
Firstly, plastic harms sea animals. Moreover, it lasts for centuries.

57
00:03:08.183 --> 00:03:10.856
On the other hand, paper bags cost more.

58
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.237
In conclusion, the ban is a good idea.

59
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:22.099
Use 'Firstly' and 'Moreover' to add points, 'On the other hand' and 'However' to show the other side, and 'In conclusion' to finish.

60
00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:26.861
Be careful! Don't say: Moreover, on the other hand, I agree.

61
00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.519
Say: On the other hand, some people disagree.

62
00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:34.539
'On the other hand' introduces the opposite side.

63
00:03:35.333 --> 00:03:37.974
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:39.884
Let's Debate!.

65
00:03:40.184 --> 00:03:41.951
A debate begins with a motion.

66
00:03:42.967 --> 00:03:45.988
Firstly, each team presents its argument with evidence.

67
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.149
Moreover, speakers must be clear and persuasive.

68
00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:54.015
On the other hand, the other team gives a rebuttal.

69
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.894
In conclusion, good debaters always show respect.

70
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.944
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:03.783 --> 00:04:07.573
blank, plastic harms animals. Moreover, it lasts long.

72
00:04:07.873 --> 00:04:11.666
A, Firstly. B, However. C, In conclusion.

73
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.432
The answer is A: Firstly.

74
00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:21.663
An answer that shows the other side is wrong is a blank.

75
00:04:21.963 --> 00:04:25.384
A, rebuttal. B, motion. C, audience.

76
00:04:28.933 --> 00:04:30.968
The answer is A: rebuttal.

77
00:04:32.117 --> 00:04:34.395
Able to make people agree means blank.

78
00:04:34.695 --> 00:04:38.766
A, persuasive. B, respectful. C, evidence.

79
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.323
The answer is A: persuasive.

80
00:04:45.533 --> 00:04:48.685
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.921
Which global issue would you like to debate?

82
00:05:00.717 --> 00:05:02.194
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:02.494 --> 00:05:12.811
I would like to debate whether social media should have an age limit. Firstly, it affects mental health. On the other hand, it helps young people learn.

84
00:05:13.111 --> 00:05:14.821
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:15.717 --> 00:05:20.319
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and linking words for arguments.

86
00:05:20.619 --> 00:05:25.222
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

87
00:05:25.522 --> 00:05:28.302
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

88
00:05:28.602 --> 00:05:31.197
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

